WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.850
An agent can do useful work.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.250
It still needs a limit.

3
00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:05.950
This is Allowance.

4
00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:08.350
Start with a task, choose the tools,

5
00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:10.800
and set how much the agent can spend.

6
00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:13.480
In the policy lab, four cents covers

7
00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:16.300
a wallet snapshot and a transaction explanation.

8
00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:19.200
A second explanation would take us over budget,

9
00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:20.250
so it’s blocked.

10
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.500
Bring the per-request limit down to one cent,

11
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:25.400
and the plan changes right away.

12
00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:28.050
You can also turn a tool off entirely.

13
00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:32.700
The workspace keeps runs, payments,
and setup in their own places.

14
00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:35.650
Review an outcome, inspect the decision,

15
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:37.050
and save the record.

16
00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:39.400
This tour moves no funds.

17
00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:42.450
Live runs use the connected operator backend,

18
00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:45.950
where payments must pass the policy checks
before signing.

19
00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:48.700
Useful tools. Clear limits.

20
00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:50.500
Every decision recorded.

21
00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:52.040
That’s Allowance.
